# Per-experiment .gitignore files live alongside their experiments
# (e.g. experiments/openevolve_milestones/.gitignore for spike-specific
# runtime outputs). Keeps the root .gitignore project-wide-only.

# autoresearch sweep dashboards — regenerable from results.jsonl via
# experiments.experiment_progress.plot_progress() and from cross-sweep
# results via experiments.plot_comparisons. Each progress.html is ~4.7 MB
# (Plotly+CDN inlined); committing them bloats the repo with derived data.
# The .jsonl files alone are sufficient for plot reproducibility.
experiments/**/progress.html
experiments/**/progress.png
experiments/**/progress_static.png
# Exception: the canonical committed-PNG location per CLAUDE.md
# (`experiments/progress/<config>/progress.png` is the PR-body screenshot).
!experiments/progress/**/progress.png

# PR-specific rolling-comment pointer files (autoresearch convention):
# stores the GitHub issue/PR comment ID that ``post_retro.py``-style scripts
# PATCH each run. Per-PR — pointers go stale the moment the PR merges.
experiments/**/.retro_comment_id

# Per-PR ad-hoc orchestration scripts. These wrap ``uv run python run.py``
# with sed-mutations of the agent/env configs for a single retest, then
# call append.py + post_retro.py. They're useful while a PR's sweep chain
# is in flight but become dead weight once the PR merges. Keep them in
# the PR worktree only; don't commit to master.
#
# Pattern is intentionally broad (matches run_chain.sh, run_stage_*.sh,
# validate_*.sh, run_baseline_*.sh, etc). If a script in this layer is
# genuinely durable (i.e. callable across PRs), promote it to
# ``experiments/scripts/`` or upstream into ``autoresearch.sweep_runner``
# rather than overriding this rule.
experiments/pr*/run_*.sh
experiments/pr*/validate_*.sh
experiments/pr*/**/run_*.sh
experiments/pr*/**/validate_*.sh
experiments/*_check*/run_*.sh
experiments/v14*/run_*.sh

# PR-specific post-retro / render / append scripts. Same rationale —
# the autoresearch package + experiment_progress provide the durable
# helpers; per-PR copies hardcode PR_NUM / ORDER / paths and break the
# moment the PR closes.
experiments/pr*/post_retro.py
experiments/pr*/render_progress.py
experiments/pr*/append.py